WEBVTT

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:05.570
Dragons once lived in that land.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:11.530
Though one may doubt that there were truly pacts between man and dragon,

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:17.530
even in this age of science, there is no questioning the existence of dragons

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:21.670
and of those with the duty of
protecting them: Dragon Dentists.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:22.440
Bridge!

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.570
Flagship Daboiyasseri has raised its battle flag!

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.780
The Lagart has also raised its battle flag!

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.720
The Lagart from DesRon 4 is flashing signals!

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.110
They've crossed the course correction point!

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.570
Five degrees starboard.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.420
Prepare to fire torpedoes!

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.270
DesRon 4 is in the vanguard, maintaining line ahead of combat formation,

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.150
and increasing speed!

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.710
Signal from the flagship!

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.020
Still unable to detect the enemy!

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:02.160
All ships, prepare for combat! Maintain radio silence!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.600
Understood. Signal the flagship in the affirmative. Relay the message to all ships.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.920
Signaling affirmation to flagship! Contacting other ships!

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.280
Cannon flame sighted!

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.030
Azimuth 40 degrees!

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.090
Are you sure it wasn't just lightning?

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.440
That's just too far away.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.450
Captain, our lookouts say they still can't even see a mast over the horizon.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.300
There's no precedent for an exchange of gunfire at this range.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.010
Was DesRon 4 detected?

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.790
It's possible.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.190
But that works out well for us.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:35.790
The amount of gunfire indicated a powerful fleet containing multiple battleships.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.900
That's sure to be the enemy's main surface fleet!

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.410
And yet the enemy still doesn't know our location.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:46.620
We can follow the original plan and have DesRon 4 trap them on the port side,

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.900
while we buy time for our main fleet to get in front of the enemy.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.840
This is our chance to attack when they can't!

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.350
Message from flagship!

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.740
Follow me! Maximum combat speed!

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.680
Hard to port!

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.230
Prepare to fire starboard cannons!

00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:59.820
Luck's on our side.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.400
We can win this war!

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.450
Flagship Daboiyasseri has been sunk!

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.500
An attack?!

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.130
That cannon fire from before?

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.170
The enemy shouldn't be able to see us!

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.280
Evade to starboard!

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.170
How are they able to hit us?

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.170
Are they psychic?

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.070
Counterattack!

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:51.410
We don't know the range!
We won't be able to hit them!

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:51.990
I don't care!

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.780
Prepare to fire on unknown port side target!

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.840
Estimated distance: 30,000!

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.830
Prepare to fire on unknown port side target!

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.750
Estimated distance: 30,000!

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.620
They're exploding in mid-air?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.490
What's going on?!

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.180
There's something in the clouds.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.860
Jump in the water, or you'll go under!

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.400
Captain.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.400
Captain!

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.000
It's the power of the dragons.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.090
Why is there a Night Howler Mushi out so close to dawn?

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.820
You're up early, Nonoko.

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:19.980
Big Sis Shibana.

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:23.150
Good morning.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:24.870
What's going on?

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.180
I woke up early.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:30.060
Did you notice it too?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.010
There were Cavity Mushis running around all night.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.290
They should be asleep by now.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:38.590
You're starting to fit the role.

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:42.050
Of course. I'm a Dragon Dentist, after all.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:44.760
So it's a piece of cake for you then, huh?

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:52.350
Glow Mushis?

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.130
There are so many.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:08:58.920
Nonoko!

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:25.950
Stop, Nonoko!

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.590
That's a Revenant!

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:32.900
Is this...

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.560
a Revenant?

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:44.400
Well, damn.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:48.280
His hair is pretty.

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:01.790
Really, now?

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:04.050
A Revenant?

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:04.710
Yes.

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.580
What's a Revenant?

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.720
A bad omen.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:12.760
They say the deceased are sometimes revived

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:15.940
and sent here through a dragon's tooth, before a calamity strikes.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.440
So this dude died once?

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:21.900
We wouldn't have had to deal with it if we had just sent him back.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.450
This kid's an enemy officer.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:27.780
You think he paid money for his rank?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.890
Some rich bastard's kid.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.830
What the... where am I?

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:45.590
This is Hanagaki Yazukaou Petowamusa.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:47.210
We're aboard a dragon.

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:49.630
Dragon?

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.250
This is a dragon?

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:09.500
That means you're all Dragon Dentists!?

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:10.800
Huh?

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:18.990
All right.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:19.910
Let go!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:25.280
Don't you know it's illegal under the Third Peace Treaty to attack the unarmed?

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:28.060
What a talkative kid.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.490
Talk about whipped.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:32.910
Lucky guy, huh?

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:33.870
Let me go!

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:34.900
No.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.870
I don't want you to get hurt.

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:42.670
I don't know how you died, but your war's over now.

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:54.700
Damn it.

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:56.000
A sign of calamity?

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.580
Give me a break.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:59.590
Arisugawa is right.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:01.240
What are we going to do with him?

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.560
Are you hurt, sir?

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.550
Go-san, it's our friend, Ozawa.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.900
At least he's hard-working.

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:12.240
Hand that man over.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:13.110
Yo.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:14.300
Good morning.

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:16.360
I've received information,

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:20.490
that an enemy officer arrived on the dragon's teeth this morning.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.250
Well, that makes things quick.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:26.120
Anyone who comes out of a dragon's tooth is a Dragon Dentist.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.540
I can't let you have him.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.970
We're making him a Dentist?

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.440
He came from the dragon's teeth.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.890
So let's say he's a Dragon Dentist. Why not?

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:41.390
Godou, give me two hours — no, one hour.

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:44.740
As soon as he answers some questions, we'll set him free.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.960
You don't have that authority.

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:51.290
If it happened on the dragon's teeth, it's up to us to decide.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:55.010
We may owe the dragon for the victory in the battle at Unashiri,

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:58.410
but half of the southern territories are in enemy hands.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:01.210
We want to learn everything we can about their actions.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.690
He's just a kid.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:05.930
We won't beat him half to death or anything.

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:08.410
Nope.

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:10.720
Dentists are different from you soldiers.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:12.960
Please.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.330
You know the Dragon's Code, don't you?

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.150
Don't you want to save lives on our side?

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.530
At the cost of more enemy soldiers' lives?

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.220
Are we letting him go?

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:30.160
We can't go against the Dragon's Code.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:36.490
Nonoko, you're the one who found him.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:38.350
You teach him how to work.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:40.420
He's going to be my junior?

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.420
Yes, sir.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:44.340
I'll make him into an outstanding Dentist.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:52.060
Now then, that's our signal.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.310
Let's get to work, everyone!

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:52.950
Hey!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.840
You still haven't finished eating.

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:58.620
Your country doesn't have rice this good, does it—

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:07.750
Elder Godou told me that,

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:11.720
it's always the ones who have nowhere to return to that are chosen to be Revenants.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:19.030
It was the dragon's choice to revive you, wasn't it?

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:20.390
Not your own.

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:22.230
Big Sis.

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:25.870
But when you think about it,

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:29.480
no one's born because they want to be.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.720
You're born before you know it,

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:34.240
so you have no choice but to live.

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:38.760
You're hungry, aren't you?

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:39.620
Eat.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.620
A reserve officer at your age...

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.700
Did your parents pull some strings for you?

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:48.670
Good for you.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:52.840
My parents were army doctors.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:54.310
<i>Were?</i>

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:58.930
They died when I was little.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.100
Just like me, then.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.860
You weren't drafted, were you?

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:09.650
You got talked into military school, and you got dragged along.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.720
I'm surprised you can tell.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:14.240
He doesn't look like a soldier.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.960
There's no hint of resolve in his face.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:19.670
He can't even decide whether or not to eat.

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:24.130
So long as you're alive, you're making decisions at every moment.

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:26.240
Are you eating or not?

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:29.250
Are you going to fight or die?

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:51.820
Tasty, huh?

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:56.620
My own people turned on me.

00:16:57.770 --> 00:17:01.580
I got captured by enemy Dragon Dentists.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.750
Want to tell me your name?

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:07.250
Bell.

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.360
I'm Nonoko.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:10.960
Call me Big Sis Nonoko.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.090
And that's Big Sis Shibana.

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.680
Nonoko.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.930
All right.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.820
Bell, if you're done eating, we're getting right to work.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:25.930
We're purifying ourselves.

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:26.830
Undress.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:31.250
Not everyone can become a Dentist.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:34.690
But know this:

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:40.050
dragons cry with their teeth.

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:41.220
What?

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:47.060
Here he is.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.350
Really?

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:50.530
We're actually letting him work as a Dentist?

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:51.910
Absolutely.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:52.530
Right?

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:58.950
All kinds of critters come out of the dragon's teeth.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:01.920
I mean, you did too.

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:04.080
But it's usually these Cavity Mushis.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.630
These tiny ones are Froth Mushis.

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.040
The pointy, bigger ones are Prickly Mushis.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:17.280
They aren't normal creatures.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:21.350
They're souls waiting to be renewed, so they aren't normally harmful to people.

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:28.210
But when the war gets intense, they start forming in bigger numbers

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.940
and eat away at the dragon's teeth.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:34.340
Dragons may be invincible, but they're helpless against cavities.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.570
They lose their power.

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:40.430
The Dentists' job is to protect the dragon from cavities.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:45.040
We gather the little, feistier Cavity Mushis into bags.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.560
That's part of our job too.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:51.700
Inside bags, they turn into rocks, and they help with the cavities...

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.250
Hey, hold it there.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.760
We can use them as medicine.

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:01.600
But once in a while, there's one that glows red.

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:02.510
Watch out for those.

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.990
The red ones are called Antidents.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.520
They're super poisonous, to both people and Mushis.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:09.600
You idiot.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:12.890
It's poisonous enough to rot your arm off with the slightest touch.

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:14.860
You don't get to use it, brat.

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:19.530
Ow!

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.030
Nonoko, you little...

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:21.880
Shut up, you old fart.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.070
Mounting Mushi!

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:24.830
Middle of teeth two and three!

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:26.020
It's pretty big!

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:26.580
Run! Run!

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.500
Bell, this way, quickly!

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:31.580
Mounting Mushis get excited when they smell people!

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:36.840
Bell!

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:37.960
He's so slow!

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:45.600
You're a spry one!

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:52.910
Get him, Arisugawa!

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:01.770
Looks like you're ready to retire soon, Soutatsu.

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:03.610
I'm not that old!

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:07.460
Bell, are you all right?

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:15.150
You!

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.840
Useless new guy!

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.960
You can go clean up the droppings over there, at least.

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:22.170
Damn good-for-nothing...

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:26.810
Isn't this...

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:33.190
This is from my country.

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:35.480
Pretty.

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:40.060
Those things come out of the teeth every day too.

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:41.480
Weird, huh?

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:43.110
Who does it belong to?

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:45.320
How would I know?

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:46.950
But...

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:52.900
Look over here.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:55.170
What are these?

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.330
Tartar Mushi.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.850
They're really tough.

00:20:58.850 --> 00:21:01.510
So we chip them down a little bit every day.

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:03.180
Touch it.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:05.720
It won't bite, will it?

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:07.390
It's totally fine.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:16.730
Touching these things makes me laugh for some reason.

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:18.650
Here, give me your hand.

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:25.310
So?

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:26.750
How does it feel?

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:39.650
They're loud, aren't they?

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:44.340
You can hear the funny noise coming from inside the teeth when you touch these Mushi.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:45.350
Huh?

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:47.280
Weird, what's wrong?

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:48.440
Why are you crying?

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:52.520
It's the voices of the dead, isn't it?

00:21:54.430 --> 00:21:59.360
A lot of people die and pass through this dragon's teeth.

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:03.050
Those things from earlier belonged to the deceased.

00:22:03.790 --> 00:22:04.860
You can tell?

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:07.890
It's not just the people from your nation.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:09.730
People from my nation too.

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:14.480
I don't know if it's because they're too heavy or because they don't need it,

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:17.370
but when people die and their hearts pass through here,

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:20.880
they leave behind things they couldn't bring to the other side.

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:22.740
Wow, Bell.

00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:25.630
Just what are dragons?

00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:32.930
Are my dead mom and dad's hearts in these teeth too?

00:22:34.230 --> 00:22:35.890
I hope there's a meaning to it,

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:39.710
and to my being here.

00:24:25.040 --> 00:24:26.930
Eating again?

00:24:26.930 --> 00:24:29.480
Come on, everyone's taking a break.

00:24:29.720 --> 00:24:32.040
And don't eat standing. It's rude.

00:24:32.040 --> 00:24:33.350
Fine, I'll sit down.

00:24:39.710 --> 00:24:41.490
Here we go.

00:24:41.490 --> 00:24:43.470
We've received a new order.

00:24:43.470 --> 00:24:45.240
The dragon will be heading south

00:24:46.030 --> 00:24:48.410
to the fallen southern land of Nagamanago,

00:24:48.410 --> 00:24:49.600
the front lines.

00:24:49.600 --> 00:24:51.930
Ozawa's guys are on edge.

00:24:51.930 --> 00:24:54.790
They're even mobilizing their precious defense cavalry.

00:24:54.790 --> 00:24:57.130
Looks like that counterattack rumor is true.

00:24:57.490 --> 00:25:02.650
The cavity on tooth 60, first row,
left side, isn't doing too well lately.

00:25:02.650 --> 00:25:04.390
Thanks to that, we're short on people.

00:25:04.620 --> 00:25:07.740
We're going to assign Bell to a tooth today.

00:25:08.390 --> 00:25:09.260
You're ready, right?

00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:19.440
I just want to try working for the sake of the souls that pass through the dragon's teeth.

00:25:19.790 --> 00:25:20.710
That's enough.

00:25:20.710 --> 00:25:22.530
That's what a Dragon Dentist does.

00:25:47.510 --> 00:25:49.350
All right, Bell, lure him in.

00:25:50.310 --> 00:25:50.930
Okay!

00:25:50.930 --> 00:25:53.180
You idiot, just keep running around.

00:26:07.390 --> 00:26:08.830
You had me worried.

00:26:10.330 --> 00:26:11.200
But good job.

00:26:30.760 --> 00:26:31.760
What happened?

00:26:32.680 --> 00:26:34.050
Elder Godou!

00:26:34.050 --> 00:26:35.490
Get back, idiot!

00:26:47.800 --> 00:26:49.160
What is that?

00:26:49.160 --> 00:26:51.780
That one looks like trouble.

00:26:53.820 --> 00:26:56.210
Oh man, this is bad.

00:26:56.560 --> 00:26:58.180
It's a Tengumushi.

00:26:58.180 --> 00:26:59.000
A Tengumushi?

00:27:00.630 --> 00:27:04.300
I've been so busy, I nearly forgot.

00:27:05.420 --> 00:27:06.750
Be careful.

00:27:06.750 --> 00:27:08.060
It eats people.

00:27:08.060 --> 00:27:11.180
Last time we saw one, it killed almost all the Dentists.

00:27:11.180 --> 00:27:13.510
Why did such a scary thing show up?

00:27:13.800 --> 00:27:15.600
It must have been the Revenant.

00:27:44.090 --> 00:27:44.960
No way!

00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:47.050
What's going on?

00:27:47.690 --> 00:27:50.260
It can pass freely in and out of the teeth!

00:27:50.660 --> 00:27:52.020
That makes it even worse!

00:27:53.090 --> 00:27:54.590
Where is it coming from?

00:27:54.590 --> 00:27:55.860
It's fast!

00:27:58.070 --> 00:27:59.140
Where is it?

00:28:13.350 --> 00:28:13.990
After it!

00:28:19.570 --> 00:28:21.500
A Cavity Mushi? All the way out here?

00:28:24.320 --> 00:28:25.340
Prepare to fire!

00:28:25.340 --> 00:28:26.670
Avoid the dragon!

00:28:27.180 --> 00:28:28.290
Fire!

00:28:36.620 --> 00:28:37.600
Are you all right?

00:28:38.080 --> 00:28:39.850
It's a monster...

00:28:40.680 --> 00:28:41.790
Have your men stand down.

00:28:41.790 --> 00:28:43.060
The Dentists will take over.

00:28:47.250 --> 00:28:49.820
You told us not to meddle, and this is what happens?

00:28:50.290 --> 00:28:51.860
They're fixing the tooth down there.

00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:55.120
We're going to stop the Tengumushi here.

00:28:55.120 --> 00:28:57.870
What's happening at the root?

00:29:00.660 --> 00:29:02.140
The wound is deep in the gum.

00:29:02.140 --> 00:29:03.960
It won't be able to support the tooth's weight.

00:29:03.960 --> 00:29:07.280
Let's tie it to the neighboring teeth to support it.

00:29:07.280 --> 00:29:08.180
Shuuzou.

00:29:08.180 --> 00:29:09.250
Don't worry.

00:29:09.250 --> 00:29:10.590
Come help, new guy!

00:29:10.590 --> 00:29:11.380
Okay!

00:29:23.950 --> 00:29:25.040
What the hell are you doing?

00:29:25.040 --> 00:29:28.200
You know better than anyone how terrible the Tengumushi is.

00:29:31.320 --> 00:29:32.190
Shibana!

00:29:39.720 --> 00:29:40.830
Go-san!

00:29:41.230 --> 00:29:42.210
Don't mind me.

00:29:42.210 --> 00:29:43.210
Go after it!

00:29:48.060 --> 00:29:49.590
Oh man, this is intense!

00:29:50.110 --> 00:29:52.530
How can you be laughing?

00:29:52.530 --> 00:29:55.470
Come on, this is what it means to be alive!

00:29:57.470 --> 00:29:59.180
We need more people up top!

00:29:59.180 --> 00:30:01.070
Someone drop a rope!

00:30:01.550 --> 00:30:03.060
Don't hit the teeth!

00:30:03.370 --> 00:30:05.190
Nonoko, don't go that way!

00:30:05.190 --> 00:30:06.730
It'll be back soon!

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:11.760
It eats the healthy souls inside the teeth, but will kill anyone in its way!

00:30:15.460 --> 00:30:16.320
Tengumushi.

00:30:16.320 --> 00:30:17.660
Nonoko!

00:30:38.600 --> 00:30:39.640
What's happening?

00:30:42.530 --> 00:30:44.980
Dying sure does suck.

00:30:47.900 --> 00:30:48.980
Shuuzou!

00:30:55.990 --> 00:30:57.320
It's slowed down!

00:30:57.320 --> 00:30:59.070
Hold it down!

00:31:13.480 --> 00:31:14.800
Shuuzou!

00:31:15.300 --> 00:31:16.800
Shuuzou!

00:31:33.680 --> 00:31:34.570
Antidents.

00:31:36.290 --> 00:31:38.820
That's why the Tengumushi became paralyzed?

00:31:47.290 --> 00:31:50.080
Today was Shuuzou's time.

00:31:50.640 --> 00:31:52.200
Let's all celebrate him.

00:32:12.970 --> 00:32:13.790
Hey!

00:32:13.790 --> 00:32:14.610
It's fine.

00:32:15.950 --> 00:32:18.510
Shuuzou was a Dragon Dentist.

00:32:18.510 --> 00:32:22.580
We let the Corpse Mushis eat him and take him back into the teeth.

00:32:33.300 --> 00:32:34.260
Nonoko...

00:32:37.300 --> 00:32:42.510
Late this afternoon, Shuuzou Satou fulfilled his duties as a Dentist.

00:32:43.210 --> 00:32:46.140
We drink to celebrate his time of passing.

00:32:46.140 --> 00:32:46.890
A toast.

00:32:47.520 --> 00:32:48.720
Cheers.

00:32:49.230 --> 00:32:50.130
Cheers.

00:32:52.870 --> 00:32:54.250
This isn't right.

00:32:54.940 --> 00:32:56.650
Why are we celebrating?

00:32:59.900 --> 00:33:03.440
It's not as if Shuuzou wanted to die.

00:33:03.440 --> 00:33:05.740
He obviously wanted to live longer!

00:33:12.330 --> 00:33:13.610
He's brave.

00:33:20.260 --> 00:33:22.190
How's the bottom?

00:33:22.190 --> 00:33:23.130
Is it holding up?

00:33:28.660 --> 00:33:32.040
Aren't you sad that Shuuzou died, Nonoko?

00:33:33.240 --> 00:33:36.130
Of course, I'm sad that I won't get to see him anymore.

00:33:37.790 --> 00:33:41.540
There was another Shuuzou back there.

00:33:42.580 --> 00:33:43.960
Oh yeah.

00:33:43.960 --> 00:33:46.120
You don't know, since you're a Revenant.

00:33:47.490 --> 00:33:50.740
We Dragon Dentists have to take a test.

00:33:50.740 --> 00:33:55.080
The dragon has to choose us before we get to be a Dragon Dentist.

00:33:57.760 --> 00:34:01.720
Our "time" is what we call our own deaths.

00:34:03.270 --> 00:34:04.840
Are you dying too?

00:34:04.840 --> 00:34:06.090
Everyone dies.

00:34:07.960 --> 00:34:12.200
Dragon Dentists all know when we're going to die.

00:34:12.860 --> 00:34:17.850
I saw, in the dragon's teeth, the moment I'm going to die too.

00:34:18.580 --> 00:34:22.090
It was about half a year ago that I took the test.

00:34:24.950 --> 00:34:28.130
I used to be a cook at a tavern.

00:34:28.130 --> 00:34:32.770
I was more or less the same as everyone around me, so it wasn't like I hated it or anything.

00:34:34.710 --> 00:34:39.670
But I heard that if I became a so-called Dragon Dentist, I could have white rice every day.

00:34:39.670 --> 00:34:42.200
By the next evening, I'd left.

00:34:43.620 --> 00:34:49.230
It sounds legitimate when you call it a "test," but the test can get you killed.

00:34:49.230 --> 00:34:53.850
I had to sign a waiver, and the other people there looked really shady.

00:34:54.360 --> 00:34:59.630
I still don't know how I got so chosen so quickly.

00:35:00.250 --> 00:35:01.520
But...

00:35:02.110 --> 00:35:04.280
Listen carefully.

00:35:05.800 --> 00:35:07.450
Dragons cry with their teeth.

00:36:00.220 --> 00:36:00.720
Who are you?

00:36:05.070 --> 00:36:06.630
Are you a dragon?

00:36:07.120 --> 00:36:08.550
No.

00:36:08.550 --> 00:36:10.880
I'm the soldier who kills you.

00:36:20.060 --> 00:36:20.840
See?

00:36:21.820 --> 00:36:24.610
Hey, you're kind of good-looking though.

00:36:26.650 --> 00:36:28.070
You must be freaking out.

00:36:28.620 --> 00:36:31.020
I'm glad I got to kill you.

00:36:31.020 --> 00:36:34.740
The teeth are the dragon's only weak spot, after all.

00:36:34.740 --> 00:36:39.600
So long as the dragon's crying from its cavities, we can kill more of your kind.

00:36:40.550 --> 00:36:42.000
Are you a bad guy?

00:36:42.950 --> 00:36:44.620
We're at war.

00:36:44.620 --> 00:36:47.600
Go. Now's your chance to escape.

00:36:52.200 --> 00:36:54.680
I'm going to die, huh?

00:36:57.500 --> 00:36:59.790
You aren't the only one who's going to die.

00:36:59.790 --> 00:37:00.850
A lot of people will.

00:37:02.620 --> 00:37:06.860
I don't know why, but I feel like I understand

00:37:08.700 --> 00:37:10.820
what I need to do.

00:37:35.140 --> 00:37:38.520
You're the only one who came back out of the teeth, huh?

00:37:39.890 --> 00:37:42.240
Where are the other people who also took the test?

00:37:42.240 --> 00:37:44.850
They all became one with the dragon's teeth.

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:49.070
They must have resisted their own fates.

00:37:49.720 --> 00:37:50.760
They're brave.

00:37:53.210 --> 00:37:56.020
Alas, dragons don't allow people to resist their fates.

00:37:58.870 --> 00:38:02.600
As of now, you're a Dragon Dentist.

00:38:02.600 --> 00:38:04.790
I look forward to working with you, Boss!

00:38:05.900 --> 00:38:08.570
Until our "time," anyway.

00:38:10.060 --> 00:38:11.600
Time to work.

00:38:12.950 --> 00:38:14.200
Oh, right.

00:38:14.200 --> 00:38:15.930
What's your name?

00:38:16.510 --> 00:38:17.890
My name is...

00:38:22.580 --> 00:38:24.500
Man, it's so cold.

00:38:25.690 --> 00:38:29.160
Just so you know, I'm not going to tell you about when I die.

00:38:30.040 --> 00:38:32.940
You don't want to die either, do you, Nonoko?

00:38:34.600 --> 00:38:36.610
Why don't you try harder to live?

00:38:38.780 --> 00:38:43.890
Well, I'd love to keep eating tasty food, but I can't do that.

00:38:43.890 --> 00:38:49.580
But until that day, I'm going to work every day and have good food.

00:38:49.580 --> 00:38:51.450
That's too sad.

00:38:52.000 --> 00:38:55.130
If you know you're going to die, and you don't resist,

00:38:55.130 --> 00:38:56.680
isn't that suicide?

00:38:57.540 --> 00:39:00.510
Is the point of being alive to live as long as you can?

00:39:09.840 --> 00:39:10.730
Good work.

00:39:12.090 --> 00:39:14.780
Did Shuuzou tell you about what happened today?

00:39:15.750 --> 00:39:16.450
No.

00:39:17.080 --> 00:39:19.840
Dragon Dentists don't tell anyone.

00:39:19.840 --> 00:39:21.030
Not you, not me.

00:39:22.060 --> 00:39:23.370
Not Takemoto either.

00:39:25.200 --> 00:39:31.020
That day twelve years ago, when a Tengumushi first showed up, was Takemoto's time.

00:39:31.840 --> 00:39:34.740
Takemoto was collected.

00:39:38.040 --> 00:39:41.050
We didn't even have any Shikairazu at the time.

00:39:41.050 --> 00:39:44.550
It was thanks to him that we were barely able to take down the Tengumushi.

00:39:45.600 --> 00:39:48.640
Though you and I are the only survivors now.

00:39:49.510 --> 00:39:53.650
I was like his kid brother, and he wouldn't even tell me about it.

00:39:54.160 --> 00:39:55.570
It wasn't just Takemoto, either.

00:39:55.920 --> 00:40:00.580
Twenty-five Dragon Dentists lost their lives that day.

00:40:00.580 --> 00:40:04.780
Not one of them told anyone about it before it happened.

00:40:05.580 --> 00:40:10.610
Even if you know you're going to die, no one lives their lives in pursuit of their own fate.

00:40:13.840 --> 00:40:14.640
What's wrong?

00:40:15.270 --> 00:40:17.780
Did you promise to marry him or something?

00:40:18.570 --> 00:40:21.680
You were in love with Takemoto, weren't you?

00:40:22.580 --> 00:40:24.570
That was a long time ago.

00:40:24.570 --> 00:40:26.220
I'm not sad anymore.

00:40:48.940 --> 00:40:51.410
Go-san, what's going on?

00:40:52.050 --> 00:40:56.060
There was an explosion at the tooth just before the Tengumushi appeared.

00:40:56.780 --> 00:40:59.800
I thought it might have been the blast from when the Mushi emerged, but...

00:41:00.360 --> 00:41:02.490
Are you suggesting that Shibana did it?

00:41:03.140 --> 00:41:05.640
There's evidence that she's been hiding a Mushi too.

00:41:08.190 --> 00:41:10.600
She's been hiding it this whole time,

00:41:10.600 --> 00:41:12.790
feeding it the dragon's teeth little by little,

00:41:12.790 --> 00:41:15.650
but keeping it sealed away so that it wouldn't get too big.

00:41:15.940 --> 00:41:20.670
You and I are the only ones who know about the Tengumushi

00:41:20.670 --> 00:41:23.220
that we took down twelve years ago.

00:41:23.220 --> 00:41:28.620
You were the one who destroyed the larvae inside its belly, Shibana.

00:41:28.870 --> 00:41:30.490
Hang on a second!

00:41:30.490 --> 00:41:33.030
Shibana's young, but she's a veteran Dragon Dentist

00:41:33.030 --> 00:41:35.690
who's been in this business for longer than I have.

00:41:35.690 --> 00:41:38.590
Why would she do that?

00:41:38.590 --> 00:41:39.860
He's right!

00:41:39.860 --> 00:41:42.300
Say something, Big Sis Shibana!

00:41:42.300 --> 00:41:45.200
We worked really hard together.

00:41:45.200 --> 00:41:48.350
You'd never hurt the dragon's teeth!

00:41:48.630 --> 00:41:52.100
Is there any meaning to a life spent waiting for your own death?

00:41:54.290 --> 00:41:55.740
You're a Dentist!

00:41:55.740 --> 00:41:57.480
You do great work.

00:41:59.010 --> 00:42:02.570
The Shibana that the dragon chose no longer... exists!

00:42:09.800 --> 00:42:12.500
It's a Tengumushi larva!

00:42:12.500 --> 00:42:14.420
Sh-Sh-Sh-Sh...

00:42:14.420 --> 00:42:15.870
Big Sis Shibana?!

00:42:16.830 --> 00:42:20.530
You kept a piece of the dragon's tooth in your mouth?

00:42:20.970 --> 00:42:26.790
It's the perfect place to lock up a Tengumushi and give him fresh air every now and then.

00:42:27.300 --> 00:42:32.220
Not to mention, dragon teeth apparently fit just fine in a human mouth.

00:42:32.800 --> 00:42:35.450
You were sucking on that thing for twelve years?

00:42:35.450 --> 00:42:39.690
You kept Takemoto's sworn enemy in your mouth as a dear pet for twelve years?

00:42:39.690 --> 00:42:41.570
You must not have noticed,

00:42:41.570 --> 00:42:44.380
but you probably touched it with the tip of your tongue too.

00:42:44.840 --> 00:42:46.360
Although that was quite a while ago.

00:42:47.730 --> 00:42:52.910
It was precisely this — this absurd Dentist's way of life — that I've been savoring.

00:42:53.100 --> 00:42:56.370
Then close your mouth and receive treatment.

00:42:56.620 --> 00:42:57.780
There's still time!

00:42:58.700 --> 00:42:59.930
Impossible.

00:43:00.330 --> 00:43:01.740
I'm already... a Cavity Mushi!

00:43:01.740 --> 00:43:03.260
a Cavity Mushi!
I'm already... a Cavity Mushi!

00:43:14.640 --> 00:43:16.980
I won't let myself be bound by the dragon's fate anymore.

00:43:26.490 --> 00:43:29.280
I'm starting my own war!

00:43:32.920 --> 00:43:36.110
Dragon's teeth sure are...

00:43:36.110 --> 00:43:37.200
sweet!
Dragon's teeth sure are...

00:44:00.300 --> 00:44:01.240
Shibana!

00:44:14.120 --> 00:44:15.510
Elder Godou!

00:44:17.750 --> 00:44:19.750
You're starting to fit the role.

00:44:20.250 --> 00:44:22.000
I'm a Dragon Dentist.

00:44:22.940 --> 00:44:26.170
I won't accept living like that!

00:44:35.370 --> 00:44:37.310
The scaffolding won't last.

00:44:37.310 --> 00:44:39.340
It needs to be secured in place with rope!

00:44:45.430 --> 00:44:46.320
Nonoko!

00:45:00.740 --> 00:45:01.290
Bell!

00:45:07.610 --> 00:45:08.390
Nonoko...

00:45:08.390 --> 00:45:08.920
Bell!

00:45:19.430 --> 00:45:21.270
Nonoko!

00:45:22.790 --> 00:45:25.810
Damn, I've never heard of anything like this!

00:45:26.330 --> 00:45:29.120
A dragon's tooth falling to the ground?

00:45:29.540 --> 00:45:31.900
Well, what happens, happens.

00:45:31.900 --> 00:45:34.100
We can only do what we can do.

00:45:36.290 --> 00:45:38.450
Let the soldiers take care of the Dentists who fell.

00:45:38.920 --> 00:45:40.630
We're going to treat the teeth.

00:45:52.120 --> 00:45:53.300
All according to plan.

00:45:54.110 --> 00:45:57.890
Now let's go check out the dragon's tooth.
